Env-gated skip of the layout-time style-resolver full reset (WEBKIT_SKIP_LAYOUT_RESOLVER_RESET).

LocalFrameViewLayoutContext::updateStyleForLayout() has a FIXME (rdar://problem/36670246):
when the style resolver doesn't exist at layout time it calls the heavyweight
Scope::didChangeStyleSheetEnvironment() (clears shared shadow-tree resolvers, invalidates
the cached CSS parser context, and schedules a full-document restyle). Device WEBKIT_STYLE_LOG
data shows this is by far the dominant source of full style-resolver Reconstructs during a
heavy load — ~990 firings per franceinfo load with the resolver merely lazily-cleared — and
CSS style resolution is ~44% of the load's main-thread time (gdb sampling). The function ends
with document->updateStyleIfNeeded(), which rebuilds the resolver lazily regardless, so the
heavyweight reset may be redundant here.

This adds WEBKIT_SKIP_LAYOUT_RESOLVER_RESET=1 to skip the reset, for an on-device A/B of DCL
and (critically) visual correctness before committing to the behaviour — the FIXME guards a
real past bug, so default unset preserves stock behaviour.

--- a/Source/WebCore/page/LocalFrameViewLayoutContext.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/page/LocalFrameViewLayoutContext.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 #include "ScriptDisallowedScope.h"
 #include "Settings.h"
 #include "StyleScope.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <wtf/SetForScope.h>
 #include <wtf/SystemTracing.h>
 #include <wtf/TZoneMallocInlines.h>
@@ -659,7 +660,18 @@
     Ref document = *this->document();
 
     // FIXME: This shouldn't be necessary, but see rdar://problem/36670246.
-    if (!document->styleScope().resolverIfExists())
+    // When the style resolver is missing at layout time this fires the heavyweight
+    // didChangeStyleSheetEnvironment() (clears shared shadow resolvers, invalidates the
+    // cached CSS parser context, and schedules a full-document restyle). On a heavy load
+    // the resolver is repeatedly lazily-cleared, so this runs ~990x/franceinfo-load, each
+    // forcing a full restyle. updateStyleIfNeeded() below rebuilds the resolver lazily
+    // anyway; WEBKIT_SKIP_LAYOUT_RESOLVER_RESET=1 skips the heavyweight reset to measure
+    // whether it is redundant here (default unset = stock behaviour, keeps the rdar fix).
+    static bool skipLayoutResolverReset = [] {
+        const char* v = getenv("WEBKIT_SKIP_LAYOUT_RESOLVER_RESET");
+        return v && *v && *v != '0';
+    }();
+    if (!document->styleScope().resolverIfExists() && !skipLayoutResolverReset)
         document->styleScope().didChangeStyleSheetEnvironment();
 
     // Viewport-dependent media queries may cause us to need completely different style information.
